by-income/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120187370272092163/kRBextYh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120187370272092163/kRBextYh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "A Look at the Wider Divide in Credit Card Delinquency by Income - Liberty Street Economics", "unwound_url": "https://libertystreeteconomics.newyorkfed.org/2026/11/a-look-at-the-wider-divide-in-credit-card-delinquency-by-income/", "url": "https://t.co/j0hc7f6R7y"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/cK10EemMvm", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120577329483383081/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120577319588790272", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/cK10EemMvm"}]}, "id": "2120577329483383081", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 6035, "like_count": 37, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Credit cards originated during 2020–22 experienced a sharp rise in serious delinquencies in 2023–24, potentially reflecting weaker borrower credit quality at origination. However, their contribution to new delinquencies has since diminished.\n\nSource: https://t.co/j0hc7f6R7y https://t.co/cK10EemMvm", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120577329483383081"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:59:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120577165242884542"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The pharmaceutical company said it has been taken off a Pentagon list of Chinese companies that the U.S. says have ties to the Chinese military.", "display_url": "wsj.com/business/wuxi-…", "end": 94, "expanded_url": "https://www.wsj.com/business/wuxi-apptec-removed-from-pentagons-list-of-chinese-military-companies-275a6a36", "images": [{"height": 640, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120024382806409216/JyHpOR5z?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120024382806409216/JyHpOR5z?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 71, "status": 200, "title": "WuXi AppTec Removed From Pentagon’s List of Chinese Military Companies", "unwound_url": "https://www.wsj.com/business/wuxi-apptec-removed-from-pentagons-list-of-chinese-military-companies-275a6a36", "url": "https://t.co/xECV14vowH"}]}, "id": "2120577165242884542", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1717, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "WuXi AppTec Removed From Pentagon’s List of Chinese Military Companies\nhttps://t.co/xECV14vowH", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120577165242884542"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:46:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120573791231430961"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/larry_kudlow/s…", "end": 96, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/larry_kudlow/status/2120557938292969773", "start": 73, "url": "https://t.co/xCWZdnizZu"}]}, "id": "2120573791231430961", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 5900, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120557938292969773", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Hope gasparino wrong that Jensen huang will have to resign. Grim segment https://t.co/xCWZdnizZu", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120573791231430961"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:25:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120568607361098039"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "China to build world-leading accounting system in next five years-", "display_url": "english.news.cn/20261111/2c769…", "end": 154, "expanded_url": "https://english.news.cn/20261111/2c7699a4d5c24e06bf7d739c289486dc/c.html", "start": 131, "status": 200, "title": "China to build world-leading accounting system in next five years", "unwound_url": "https://english.news.cn/20261111/2c7699a4d5c24e06bf7d739c289486dc/c.html", "url": "https://t.co/lTAMKW2p1h"}]}, "id": "2120568607361098039", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 17330, "like_count": 98, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "Xinhua: “China will strive to build an accounting system with Chinese characteristics that is internationally leading in 2026-30.”\nhttps://t.co/lTAMKW2p1h", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2120568607361098039"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:18:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120566766598496482"], "id": "2120566766598496482", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 142, "impression_count": 41758, "like_count": 523, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 109}, "text": "Bloomberg: “Russia has effectively abandoned attempts to replace the dollar with China’s yuan under the pressure of US secondary sanctions, underlining the difficulties facing other nations looking for an alternative global currency.”\n\nAs I’ve long explained, surplus countries", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2120566766598496482"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:53:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120560637495644490"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Fu7Sx0UBz0", "end": 246, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120560637495644490/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120560620898861056", "start": 223, "url": "https://t.co/Fu7Sx0UBz0"}]}, "id": "2120560637495644490", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 7254, "like_count": 63, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "Indeed job postings:\n\n1/ The surge in US software development postings continues - we're at the highest level in over 3 years, though still about a year away at current growth rates (~24% Y/Y) from the pre-pandemic levels. https://t.co/Fu7Sx0UBz0", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120560637495644490"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:38:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120556908734025806"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 81, "start": 75, "tag": "China"}, {"end": 272, "start": 269, "tag": "AI"}]}, "id": "2120556908734025806", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1529, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"When world leaders fly into Shenzhen next wk, they may catch a glimpse of #China's vision for the future of global trade: a high-tech port humming w/next-gen hardware &amp; software...The Mawan Terminal—complete w/its driverless trucks, remote-controlled cranes &amp; #AI-powered", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120556908734025806"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:19:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120551997531414835"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/fMWzpzprHN", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120551997531414835/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120551982180216832", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/fMWzpzprHN"}]}, "id": "2120551997531414835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 6139, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "1/ Since real wage growth discourse is back, a reminder: using headline inflation introduces a lot of noise.\n\nIt's fine for some uses (what's happening very recently) but less useful if you're interested in trends.\n\nMuch of the recent real wage growth weakening won't persist. https://t.co/fMWzpzprHN", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120551997531414835"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:55:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120545875130769452"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 233, "id": "21232827", "start": 221, "username": "RyanDetrick"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/bDYgpbq3fk", "end": 257, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120545875130769452/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120545781165797378", "start": 234, "url": "https://t.co/bDYgpbq3fk"}]}, "id": "2120545875130769452", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 29, "impression_count": 9090, "like_count": 70, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Since 2000, stocks have returned an average of 7.7% annually, but missing the 10 best trading days each year would have turned that gain into a 15.4% average annual loss, highlighting the risks of market timing.\n\nSource: @RyanDetrick https://t.co/bDYgpbq3fk", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120545875130769452"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:50:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120539671335780835", "2120544597961240583"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/axios/status/2…", "end": 63, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/axios/status/2120535941043646555", "start": 40, "url": "https://t.co/8TGXdjo5Ki"}]}, "id": "2120544597961240583", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 5945, "like_count": 56, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120535941043646555", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Bessent throwing lutnick under the bus? https://t.co/8TGXdjo5Ki", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120544597961240583"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:30:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120539671335780835", "2120544597961240583"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/axios/status/2…", "end": 63, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/axios/status/2120535941043646555", "start": 40, "url": "https://t.co/8TGXdjnxUK"}]}, "id": "2120539671335780835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1724, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120535941043646555", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Bessent throwing nutlick under the bus? https://t.co/8TGXdjnxUK", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120539671335780835"}, {"author_id": "3039504459", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:15:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120535814035603590"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A memory phenomenon known as the anomalous Kovacs effect has been experimentally observed in a granular system for the first time.", "display_url": "go.aps.org/4Aku6Tj", "end": 275, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/4Aku6Tj", "images": [{"height": 200, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120535818267693057/f1Gzldpg?format=png&name=orig", "width": 200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120535818267693057/f1Gzldpg?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 252, "status": 200, "title": "Kovacs Memory Effect in a Thin Granular Layer: Experimental Evidence and Its Physical Origin", "unwound_url": "https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/791d-2tx9", "url": "https://t.co/mPUwolPfmD"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/sRYbRr9ExS", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2120535814035603590/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120535811078737921", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/sRYbRr9ExS"}]}, "id": "2120535814035603590", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 11328, "like_count": 99, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 20}, "text": "High-speed cameras capture a brief temperature dip in a vertically shaken granular fluid during its initial relaxation. Simulations and kinetic theory link this Kovacs memory effect to coupling between horizontal and vertical temperatures.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/mPUwolPfmD https://t.co/sRYbRr9ExS", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2120535814035603590"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:12:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120535260131889273"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/chriscillizza/…", "end": 179, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/chriscillizza/status/2119988541317140724", "start": 156, "url": "https://t.co/sRQBevmgi6"}]}, "id": "2120535260131889273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3164, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119988541317140724", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Am I weird for thinking that this visualization, while visually striking, is clunky at info transmission?\n\nThe counties should be sized by vote margin imho https://t.co/sRQBevmgi6", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120535260131889273"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:51:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120514689805295657"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Updated August 2026. This dashboard now runs V3: an open-weights judge (Llama 3.3 70B), a deduplicated corpus, and revised TrueSkill statistics. The original Gemini-Flash-era dashboard is preserved at /fedlock/v2/. See Methodology for what changed. Scores are era-adjusted: each speech is measured against the quarterly average, then re-centered to 50. This separates a speaker’s dispositional hawkishness from the era they spoke in. The most recently delivered speeches in the tournament, newest first.", "display_url": "thestalwart.com/fedlock/", "end": 270, "expanded_url": "https://thestalwart.com/fedlock/", "images": [{"height": 1084, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120514738626981888/R8a_Zzqa?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1905}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120514738626981888/R8a_Zzqa?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 247, "status": 200, "title": "FedLock: FOMC Hawkishness", "unwound_url": "https://thestalwart.com/fedlock/", "url": "https://t.co/zVh6WKpRAj"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/iet4mpU0Rb", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120514689805295657/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120514478315823104", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/iet4mpU0Rb"}, {"display_url": "x.com/donnelly_brent…", "end": 318, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/donnelly_brent/status/2120161377247469967", "start": 295, "url": "https://t.co/CZnm3qKXTi"}]}, "id": "2120514689805295657", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 23415, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120161377247469967", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This chart matches Fedlock, which also identifies yesterday's speech as Waller's most hawkish since 2023. There's no \"ground truth\" with measuring sentiment like this, but it's not to see my approach roughly align with other, existing techniques. https://t.co/zVh6WKpRAj https://t.co/iet4mpU0Rb https://t.co/CZnm3qKXTi", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120514689805295657"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:18:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120506383678509186"], "id": "2120506383678509186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 107602, "like_count": 530, "quote_count": 16, "reply_count": 33, "retweet_count": 25}, "text": "*ANTHROPIC MEGA-IPO IS SAID TO BE MULTIPLE TIMES OVERSUBSCRIBED", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120506383678509186"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:10:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120504367652491396"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/zachary/status…", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/zachary/status/2120360815932944838", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/7Rhe0WswrN"}]}, "id": "2120504367652491396", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 32, "impression_count": 21320, "like_count": 57, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120360815932944838", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“A person granted anonymity to discuss Nvidia’s strategy said the company is moving away from the “aggressive elements of the approach” that it once took in Washington. The person attributed the shift to new leadership